    "probe_text": "I now have the full create path. Here is the complete, ordered account of what happens on `POST /api/owners` \u2014 handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:109`).\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Before the controller body (Spring MVC / framework)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else 403.\n2. **Body deserialization + Bean Validation** \u2014 the generated `OwnersApi.addOwner` annotates the body `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (`OwnersApi.java:86`), so JSR-380 validation runs on `OwnerFieldsDto` before the method executes. Any failure \u21d2 400. Constraints (field order among these is not deterministic):\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max 10)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)` (only when present)\n   - `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)` (only when present)\n   - `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^\\D*(\\d\\D*){10}$)` (exactly 10 digits), `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Email`, `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `registrationDate` \u2014 `@PastOrPresent`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n   - **Class-level `@PostcodeValidation`** \u2014 if a 4-digit postcode is present *and* the city resolves to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), the postcode must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Unknown city or absent postcode passes.\n   - **Class-level `@AddressPresenceValidation`** \u2014 at least one of `addressLine1` or `address` must be non-blank.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Controller body\n\n3. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`), which performs several *normalizing side-effects*:\n   - **Telephone \u2192 E.164** (`E164.toE164`): strips non-digits; a leading `+` is kept as an explicit country code, otherwise `+61` is assumed and a single leading `0` dropped; result must be 8\u201315 digits (and `+61`\u21d29, `+1`\u21d210 national digits). **Invalid input throws `IllegalArgumentException`** here (would surface as 500), not a clean 400.\n   - **Address normalization** (`Addresses.normalize` on line1/line2): trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`.\n   - **Address composition** (`Addresses.compose`): the stored `address` is built preferring `addressLine1` (+`addressLine2`), falling back to the flat `address`, all normalized.\n   - **Email lower-cased** via `Owner.setEmail`.\n   - `id` and `pets` are ignored (not mapped).\n4. **Disposable-email block** \u2014 `DisposableDomains.isBlocked(owner)`: if the email domain is `mailinator.com` / `tempmail.com` / `guerrillamail.com` \u21d2 **400**.\n5. **Load all existing owners** \u2014 `clinicService.findAllOwners()` (used by all checks below).\n6. **Daily registration cap** \u2014 `DailyRegistrations.countOn(owners, today) >= 100` \u21d2 **429**. Count is by owners whose `registrationDate` equals today rolled to a business day.\n7. **Per-city cap** \u2014 `CityCodes.count(owners, owner) >= 50` (same city, case-insensitive) \u21d2 **409**.\n8. **Assign household id** (side-effect) \u2014 `owner.setHouseholdId(Households.householdId(owner))`: first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode`.\n9. **Identity-key duplicate check** \u2014 `IdentityKeys.isDuplicate`: rejects if a non-deleted existing owner shares the whole key `telephone|email|householdId` \u21d2 **409**.\n10. **Household duplicate check** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold == true`, `Households.isDuplicate` rejects if a non-deleted owner shares the same household id (same last name +